+### What a released machine carries: `audio` and `notes` in status
+
+Release keeps the guest as it is, including settings made inside it. So that
+the next session sees this **before** it starts the machine, `./vm.sh status`
+shows for every machine its effective `audio` mode and a `notes` list, read
+from `machines.<name>.notes` (a list of strings) in the local configuration.
+Whoever changes something inside a guest that outlives the session - sound
+output, AHI or other preferences, installed software, data left on `SYS:` -
+adds a dated line there, with that machine stopped. Remove a line when the
+change is undone.
+
 Growth: at 44.1 kHz stereo 16-bit a machine playing continuously writes about
 10 MB a minute to its `audio.wav`.
 
